  "routing_rules": [
    "Do not create multiple user inboxes; SIEZEALL 00_INBOX_USER is the single user reference intake surface.",
    "HNS Drive is internal/admin master and is not a user file-drop surface.",
    "SIEZEALL Drive is user-facing distribution/sync and user reference intake.",
    "GitHub stores code/governance/schema/contracts/manifests; do not use GitHub as the default binary asset or learning-data current store.",
    "Netlify delivers PWA shell/runtime only and never decides asset-to-slot binding.",
    "Asset slot binding is frozen before distribution by manifest + SHA-256; PWA verifies and caches the approved package.",
    "Local collector may watch the synced SIEZEALL inbox path but stops after Mining dispatch; Indexing/Learning remain downstream.",
    "Do not delete source material until extraction/indexing/readback has a verified receipt during the current fragmentation-cleanup phase.",
    "Preserve Drive file IDs when reorganizing; prefer move/rename over copy/delete.",
    "Do not delete same-name items based on name alone; inspect content, parent, date and authority first.",
    "Handoff artifacts remain recovery evidence, not source of truth.",
    "Current PWA source code lives in GitHub product repositories; high-churn runtime data and binary asset masters do not.",
    "Do not place Git repositories inside synchronized Google Drive workspaces.",
    "Do not create a new TAKY sibling root when an existing role folder fits.",
    "NotebookLM material is legacy/optional and excluded from the default active route.",
    "TAKY root layout is locked to final_storage_namespace; any unexpected root child is HOLD and must be moved to TAKY/90_MAINTENANCE/90_TEMP until assigned.",
    "90_TEMP is non-authoritative quarantine/working storage and is excluded from normal canonical/runtime reads by default.",
    "TAKY root exposes only 00_CONTEXT, 10_DOMAINS, 20_PLATFORM and 90_MAINTENANCE.",
    "00_CONTEXT stays directly under TAKY root for fast cross-chat/context access.",
    "Logical role folders keep stable Drive IDs and may be physically nested under presentation groups without changing semantic ownership.",
    "Current physical paths are read from final_storage_namespace.logical_role_paths; do not reconstruct paths from historical flat layout."
  ],
